  "scope": "Exact projection in a six-qudit tensor constraint benchmark removes gauge-ray distinguishability. The finite logical Gaussian Berry coefficient has explicit cutoff errors and saturates in the infrared at fixed prime. A noncompact Gaussian rigging map repairs the prepotential state quotient but does not create a critical width from uniformly bounded Gaussian precision. The linear and cubic tensor Gaussian Hamiltonians have the same vacuum and different time response. No local finite-spin gravitational phase, nonlinear Einstein gravity, or TOE is proved. No Lean theorem."
